      "writtenOn": "2021-07-08T18:25:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What makes ramdisk_available different from recovery_available and vendor_available in this regard?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "e79dbc6202b499c28b700b5d3bbf855704503f66",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1eb9272e_b3cd31bf",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-09T15:17:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "History. We already support recovery_available and vendor_available and so they are present in both the runtime and ART prebuilts, on headers, objects and libraries. I don\u0027t know if those are needed or safe but I didn\u0027t want to make things worse by adding ramdisk_available to all of them when they didn\u0027t need it.\n\nI have been thinking that we need more fine grained control over these traits of the modules that apply to shared and static libraries and not just pass them through to the SDK snapshot just because they are specified on the source module.",
      "parentUuid": "e285c9c1_160b3c89",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "e79dbc6202b499c28b700b5d3bbf855704503f66",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5938e14_3f16ef66",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-09T15:40:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "They\u0027re not actual variants, right? Iow they cannot be built differently - all the *_available just make up a dependency control mechanism for what can go into different images? If so I think it\u0027s correct to just propagate them.\n\nThe risk with this defensive approach is that future work might be hampered by a perceived requirement to keep it working this way. If we can dispense with imageAgnostic altogether I think it\u0027d be a good thing.",
      "parentUuid": "1eb9272e_b3cd31bf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "e79dbc6202b499c28b700b5d3bbf855704503f66",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c3b4b26_86cc4f86",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-09T22:50:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e They\u0027re not actual variants, right?\n\nThey are. So, you have image:ramdisk, image:recovery etc.\n\n\u003e Iow they cannot be built differently\n\nI don\u0027t see why they can\u0027t. In order to make sure that there were no differences then you would have to make sure that any information derived from the *_available property had no impact on the compiler command line and linker command line.\n\nAFAICT we do not prevent that so for safety\u0027s sake we have to assume that they are different.",
      "parentUuid": "f5938e14_3f16ef66",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "e79dbc6202b499c28b700b5d3bbf855704503f66",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8f3eb5d2_485a6f12",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-14T00:33:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I was dead wrong. Then the problem is the opposite for the other *_available - we ought not propagate any of them without being certain their prebuilts are identical between the images, right? Or else we should split prebuilt srcs by image if any *_available is set.\n\nI guess that ought to have a ticket, but I doubt anyone will spend time on it before we have an actual problem, so not sure it\u0027s even worth filing one. Still, it\u0027d be useful to mention this unsafe behaviour next to the AddProperty calls for them, just below the mt.imageAgnostic if clause. The comment right now gives the impression there\u0027s something special with ramdisk_available wrt the others, but there\u0027s not.",
      "parentUuid": "1c3b4b26_86cc4f86",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "e79dbc6202b499c28b700b5d3bbf855704503f66",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
